  "notes": "Aerial journey north-west from Newport over the Cusick valley toward Ione, using USGS 3DEP terrain. Glacier geometry is an artistic compressed interpretation of the Pend Oreille River lobe, not a dated reconstruction; the straight axis spans the broad bent valley and bed elevation limits ice to low ground. River station coordinates from USGS NWIS 12395500, 12395950 and 12396500 (NAD83). Regional glacial context: Carrara, Kiver and Stradling (1996), https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/70018536. Forest recovery is an explicitly compressed later stage. The simplified glacier axis begins west-southwest of Newport to include the Cusick bend, and ends north of Ione; neither axis endpoint is a measured historic terminus. The sparse instanced stands over canopy reflect the mixed forest and open valley floor and keep the long flight within memory limits.",
